Product of the Last K Numbers

Problem Statement

Design a data structure that accepts a stream of integers and returns the product of the last "k" numbers in the stream.

Approach: Prefix Products

Instead of calculating the product of the last "k" numbers every time, maintain cumulative prefix products.

For a stream:
"[3, 2, 5, 4]"

Prefix products:
"[1, 3, 6, 30, 120]"

The product of the last "k" numbers can be calculated in O(1) using division:

"product(last k) = prefix[-1] // prefix[-k-1]"

Handling Zero

Zero makes prefix division invalid.

Whenever "0" is added, reset the prefix array to "[1]". This ensures all stored prefix products are calculated only after the most recent zero.

If "k" is greater than or equal to the length of the prefix array, the requested range contains a zero, so return "0".

Implementation (Python)

class ProductOfNumbers:

    def __init__(self):
        self.prefix = [1]

    def add(self, num: int) -> None:
        if num == 0:
            self.prefix = [1]
        else:
            self.prefix.append(self.prefix[-1] * num)

    def getProduct(self, k: int) -> int:
        if k >= len(self.prefix):
            return 0

        return self.prefix[-1] // self.prefix[-k-1]

Example

Input:

add(3)
add(0)
add(2)
add(5)
add(4)
getProduct(2)
getProduct(3)
getProduct(4)

Output:

20
40
0

Complexity Analysis

Operation| Time Complexity
add(num)| O(1)
getProduct(k)| O(1)

Space| Complexity
Prefix products| O(n)

Key Insight

Prefix products allow range products to be calculated using division rather than iterating over the elements. Resetting the prefix array whenever zero is encountered prevents division-by-zero issues and keeps both operations efficient.

